  "origin": "Large synthetic instruction dataset emulating retrieval of a wide variety of multilingual open sources from Common Corpus. Used to train Pleias-RAG-1B (a 1.2B-parameter Small Reasoning Model for retrieval-augmented generation, search, query routing, query reformulation, and source reranking). The dataset contains synthetic rows categorized by task type (e.g. 'memorization', 'rag'); each row records the generator model (e.g. qwen-3-8b-memorization), the source URL (mostly Wikipedia), and the source license (e.g. CC-By-SA 4.0, CC0). Form: synthetic instruction data generated by an LLM, emulating RAG retrieval over Common Corpus-derived sources. Note: this is a DIFFERENT training phase than the Pleias-1.2b-Preview base model, which was pretrained directly on Common Corpus. Pleias-RAG-1B is fine-tuned on SYNTH, which is itself derived from Common Corpus sources. This record therefore represents the SFT/RAG phase, not the pretrain phase — and it surfaces a structural gap: ProvenanceRecord has no field to distinguish *which training phase* (pretrain / SFT / RAG-grounding) a dataset was used in. That usage/metadata belongs to the model producer's view of the dataset (Mímir stress-test Gap 4), not the dataset producer's record. See notes/stress-test-pleias-common-corpus.md (Gap E). The license field carries the dataset's own Hugging Face page URL as a best-effort IRI, since SYNTH is a synthetic dataset whose per-row licenses inherit from the emulated Common Corpus sources (CC-By-SA 4.0, CC0, etc.) — another instance of Gap B (per-document multi-license aggregate).",
  "custodyChain": [
    {
      "agent": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/PleIAs/common_corpus",
      "action": "provided-emulated-open-sources",
      "startTime": "2024-11-01T00:00:00Z"
